{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 53, :comments ["<b>And the Levites shall camp around.</b> Between the camps of Israel and the Tabernacle, and they shall not allow them to approach it." "<b>And the Levites shall camp around.</b> Above, nearby, it is written ״וסביב למשכן יחנו״ — that is when the Ark sets out and when it is carried; here, when the Tabernacle is encamped." "<b>And there shall be no wrath.</b> From what it said above, ״and the stranger who approaches shall be put to death,״ as we find with Uzza." "<b>Upon the congregation of the children of Israel.</b> Upon one of the congregations of the children of Israel. For example: ״אם שלש אלה לא יעשה לה״ and ״ויקבר בערי הגלעד״ and ״ועל עיר בן אתונות״."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {3 "The three cited phrases are brought as grammatical parallels where על is read distributively ('upon one of'); Judges 10:4, 1 Chronicles 2:22, and Numbers 22:39 respectively. The second phrase reads ויקבר possibly instead of the expected ויקבץ; translated as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:17.164181730Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}